### BolusTrack_InteractiveEdit.m\
\
Full bolus tracking GUI with interactive ROI editing, metadata-based frame rate loading, and robust temporal denoising.\
\
**To use:** Rename this file to `BolusTrack.m` and place it in your MATLAB path.\
\
**Syntax:**\
```matlab\
BolusTrack\
```\
\
**GUI buttons (left panel):**\
\
| Button | Function |\
|--------|----------|\
| Load Data | Select and load a cropped bolus TIFF stack |\
| Load Metadata | Load a .txt metadata file to auto-populate the frame rate |\
| Frame Rate | Manually enter or verify the frame rate (auto-filled by Load Metadata) |\
| Import ROIs | Load a maskObj .mat file and overlay on the MIP |\
| Show ROIs tc | Generate time-courses from current ROI positions, apply denoising, and display the first trace |\
| Pop-out View | Open a full-size figure with interactive ROIs for editing |\
| Denoise (SD) | Set the outlier threshold for temporal denoising (default: 2.5) |\
\
**GUI buttons (right panel):**\
\
| Button | Function |\
|--------|----------|\
| Fit Gamma function | Fit a gamma function to the current trace |\
| Save values/next trace | Save the current fit and advance to the next ROI trace |\
| Experiment | Label the condition (e.g., "baseline" or "CO2") |\
| Subject ID | Enter the subject number |\
| Export results | Save .csv and .mat output files |\
| NaN initial Values | Reset fitting parameter fields |\
| Clear All | Clear all data from workspace and GUI |\
\
**Load Metadata:**\
\
Reads the tab-delimited .txt file exported from Fluoview during TIFF conversion. Parses the "T Dimension" line to extract the number of frames and total duration, then calculates and auto-fills the frame rate. Example parsed line:\
\
```\
"T Dimension"  "300, 0.000 - 59.004 [s], Interval FreeRun"\
  -> 300 frames / 59.004 s = 5.08 fps\
```\
\
The frame rate field remains editable so you can override if needed.\
\
**Temporal denoising:**\
\
Applied automatically when "Show ROIs tc" is clicked. For each time point in each ROI's raw trace, the algorithm compares the value to the median of a local window (10 frames on each side). If the point deviates by more than N standard deviations from that local median, it is replaced with the median. This removes cardiac and respiratory pulsation spikes while preserving the bolus passage curve shape.\
\
The threshold (default 2.5 SD) is adjustable via the "Denoise (SD)" field in the GUI. Lower values = more aggressive denoising; higher values = more permissive. The original unfiltered trace is preserved in `fitOut(n).yRawOriginal` for reference.\
\
**Pop-out View:**\
\
Opens a maximizable figure with all ROIs as interactive polygons. You can drag entire ROIs and/or individual vertices. Click "Apply Edits" to send changes back, then "Show ROIs tc" to extract time-courses with the corrected positions.\
\
**Fitting procedure (per ROI):**\
\
1. Click on the trace peak, then click in Amplitude field and press Enter\
2. Click on the time of the peak, then click in Time to Peak field and press Enter\
3. Click on the bolus onset, then click in Fit Start field and press Enter\
4. Click on the return to baseline, then click in Fit End field and press Enter\
5. Click in FWHM field and press Enter (auto-calculated)\
6. Click in Baseline shift field and press Enter (auto-calculated)\
7. Click "Fit Gamma function"\
8. If good, click "Save values/next trace"\
9. If bad, adjust parameters and re-fit\
\
**Output files (from Export results):**\
\
| File | Contents |\
|------|----------|\
| `subjectID_bolus#_condition.csv` | Gamma fit parameters for all ROIs |\
| `subjectID_bolus#_condition.mat` | fitOut struct, mask, and maskNum arrays |\
| `subjectID_bolus#_condition_MaskObj.mat` | Updated maskObj |\
\
**CSV columns:**\
\
`subj_num, ves_num, exp, InitAmp, InitT2p, InitFWHM, InitM, F_Amp, F_T2p, F_FWHM, F_M, AUC, AUCn, TTlb, TTm, TThb, OnTSc, ROI size`\
\
Where: `F_` = fitted parameter, `Init` = initial estimate, `TT` = transit time (lb/m/hb = lower bound/mean/higher bound), `OnTSc` = onset time scaled to earliest onset, `AUCn` = normalized AUC.}